{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Communication","abstract":[{"text":"The Swift language is developed in the open, and all technical or administrative topics about the language or community processes should be directed to the Swift public forums. Public conversations are encouraged, and active developers of the Swift language should monitor the relevant forum categories.","type":"text"}],"title":"Communication","identifiers":["doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/forums","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/reporting-bugs","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/triaging-bugs","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/good-first-issues","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-evolution","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/contributing-code","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/contributor-ladder"]},{"anchor":"LLVM-and-Swift","title":"LLVM and Swift","identifiers":["doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/llvm-and-swift"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift.org community has the singular goal of making the world’s best general purpose programming language. Collectively we will develop the language in the open, with contributions from anyone who wishes to participate. This guideline document describes how the Swift community is organized so that we can work together to add amazing new capabilities to Swift, and make it available to even more developers across more platforms."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/contributing-to-swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Contributing to Swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Everyone is welcome to contribute to Swift.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Contributing doesn’t just mean submitting pull requests – there are many different ways for you to get involved, including answering questions on the forums, reporting or triaging bugs, and participating in the Swift evolution process."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No matter how you want to get involved, we ask that you first learn what’s expected of anyone who participates in the project by reading the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.swift.org\/code-of-conduct\/","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-groups","doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/github-policies"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://project-operations/documentation/project-operations/swift-groups":{"abstract":[{"text":"Three types of groups play an integral role in shaping Swifts development: Workgroups, Steering Groups, and the Core Team.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-groups","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Swift Groups","identifier":"doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-groups"},"doc://project-operations/documentation/project-operations/swift-evolution":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-evolution","title":"Swift Evolution","identifier":"doc:\/\/project-operations\/documentation\/project-operations\/swift-evolution","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the process the Swift project uses to evolve the language."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://project-operations/documentation/project-operati